cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Conditional mutual information of adjacent intervals as a
  quantum-Markov defect
message: >-
  If you use this work, cite the papers rather than the repository
  where possible; the repository is the working record behind them.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Stottmeister
    given-names: Alexander
    affiliation: >-
      Institut für Theoretische Physik, Leibniz Universität Hannover
repository-code: https://github.com/alexander-stottmeister/cft-cmi
abstract: >-
  For three adjacent intervals in the vacuum of a chiral conformal field theory
  the Longo-Xu conditional mutual information is finite and strictly positive.
  This project reads that number as the failure of a Petz recovery map,
  constructs the recovery channel at zero collar width in the type-III setting,
  and measures how well it works: an exact quadratic law for the free fermion,
  universality of its coefficient for every diffeomorphism-covariant net, the
  second-order optimum over all recovery channels, and a corner calculus for
  sequential recovery along a chain of intervals.
keywords:
  - conformal field theory
  - conditional mutual information
  - Petz recovery map
  - operator algebras
  - quantum Markov chains
license: CC-BY-4.0
license-url: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
